Return `false` from the `_.transform` iteratee to stop iteration early.

```js
_.transform([2, 3, 4], function (result, n) {
  result.push(n *= n);
  return n % 2 === 0;
}, []);

// => [4, 9]
```

The callback receives `(accumulator, value, key, object)`. Mutate the accumulator as needed; returning `false` is the early-exit signal.
